        "original_id": "e3f584d5-9f16-5f31-a0bd-b7e9f7d400ce",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hetfield, Rick Rubin, Bob Rock\n- Organizations: Metallica\n- Products: \"Enter Sandman\", \"Metallica\" (album), Death Magnetic\n- Concepts: child's nightmares\n\nFacts:\n- In 1991, Metallica released the album \"Metallica\".\n- The album \"Metallica\" produced five well-known singles: \"Enter Sandman\", \"The Unforgiven\", \"Nothing Else Matters\", \"Wherever I May Roam\", and \"Sad but True\".\n- \"Enter Sandman\" is a song by the American heavy metal band Metallica.\n- Hetfield, Metallica's vocalist and rhythm guitarist, wrote the lyrics to \"Enter Sandman\".\n- The lyrics of \"Enter Sandman\" deal with the concept of a child's nightmares.\n- Death Magnetic was Metallica's first album produced by Rick Rubin.\n- Death Magnetic was Metallica's first album since \"Metallica\" (1991) not produced by Bob Rock.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
